# Docker build context exclusions. BOTH images build from the repo root as their
# context (./Dockerfile and ./cv-service/Dockerfile, see docker-compose.yml), so this
# one file governs both — hence the `!` re-include for the fat jar below.
#
# WHY this exists: without it the context was 2.8 GB, of which the cv-service image
# needs ~150 MB. The 1.7 GB virtualenv alone was being tarred and shipped to the
# daemon on every build; combined with a 96%-full disk that is what exhausted it
# during the MEDIA-SOT measurement run.

# Java build output — but the root Dockerfile copies the fat jar OUT of it, so that
# one path is re-included. Order matters: the later rule wins.
**/target
!station/vision-app/target/vision-app-*.jar

# Frontend: the jar already contains the built SPA (frontend-maven-plugin), so no
# image ever needs the sources or the toolchain.
**/node_modules
station/vision-web/dist
station/vision-web/.angular

# Python: the cv-service image builds its own environment with pip, and downloads
# its own yolo11n weights. A host venv in the context is pure freight.
cv/cv-service/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
.pytest_cache

# CV working data: training runs, datasets, and throwaway spikes/demos are developer
# artifacts, never image content.
cv/cv-service/runs
cv/cv-service/datasets
cv/cv-service/spikes
cv/cv-service/demo

# Repo furniture no Dockerfile copies.
.git
.github
.idea
.claude
docs
contexts
infra
clips
data
*.iml
